>Maybe you can tell me: what happens lockfile-wise if you start a 27th game?
>Since the first set go [a-z]lock, what would the last one end up being?

unixunix.c implements a hard limit of 25; actually you never get up to
zlock.

        if(locknum) {
                if(locknum > 25) locknum = 25;

However, if MAXNROFPLAYERS is not set in the initial shell script, if
(locknum) isn't true, and it simply prevents 2 games being started under
the same character name and with the same UID. Since as I understand it a
tournament player's characters are named after their tournament username
and we have separate UNIX UIDs on the tournament servers, it should be
perfectly safe just to comment out the line that sets MAXNROFPLAYERS. By
doing so I have 30 NetHacks running at home right now.

Of course, you may want to get a second opinion on that one and/or just
chase up more servers.
